function ansMethod(){return `<p><b>The agent reads the facts from the source files. Fixed rules then calculate every figure.</b></p><ul><li>Expected total cost = cost spent so far + cost still to be spent.</li><li>Profit margin = (contract value \u2212 expected total cost) \u00F7 contract value.</li><li>Profit at risk = the gap between the target and the forecast margin \u00D7 contract value.</li><li>Unbilled work = hours on unapproved work \u00D7 the agreed hourly rate.</li><li>Days late = expected date \u2212 promised date.</li></ul><p><b>A project is RED when</b> its margin is 8 or more points below target; or the client has made a formal complaint or a penalty applies; or unbilled work is \u20B90.50 Cr or more, or 3% of the contract value or more; or a promised date is 30 or more days late, or 10 or more days late with a payment linked.</p><p><b>A project is AMBER when</b> its margin is 3 to 8 points below target; or service targets are missed repeatedly; or there is any smaller unbilled amount; or a promised date is 10 to 29 days late.</p><p>A missing value is shown as \u201CNot reported\u201D and is never estimated.</p>`}
